This section is not intended as review on different numerical schemes; rather it is an attempt to
identify where the current state-of-the-art stands in terms of validated predictive capability, i.e.,
based on comparison to experiments. Computational approaches depend to a large extent on the
particular problem as well as on the corresponding Reynolds number range. For example, at
small MAV or NAV scales typical of insect flight 2 4
