advantages: the orifices do not materially modify the blade geometry; and blowing can be
initiated on-demand, within the rotor cycle, using on-off control (see section 3.9.1), for example.
It can therefore potentially be employed in a close-loop control scheme, that initiates blowing
at incipient stall. Two technological challenges to be considered are the physical supply of
compressed air into the rotating blades, and estimation of the net gains when using engine bleed
