4.3 Excitation-Based Actuation
To date, no convincing experimental demonstrations of excitation-based dynamic stall control
have been performed for M  0.3. However, static experiments performed with DBD plasma
actuators [276,277]—both AC and nanosecond pulsed-DC—and hover results with nanosecond
pulsed-DC at M tip = 0.3 [278] suggest that beneficial performance results can be obtained.
